	abstract = {This paper considers the problem of testing for parameter changes in structural vector autoregressive (SVAR) models via using the independent component analysis (ICA). For this task, we first transform the SVAR model into a vector autoregressive (VAR) model and estimate the VAR estimates. Then, we transform the VAR model again to an SVAR model with independent errors using the ICA method. This ICA method is hybridized with the cumulative sum (CUSUM) test developed for location-scale time series models. In this paper, we also consider the maximum likelihood estimator (MLE)-based CUSUM test and derive its limiting null distribution for providing a theoretical background on the CUSUM test. Our empirical studies affirm the validity of the CUSUM test based on both methods in various situations and particularly exhibit the excellency of the ICA method in terms of computing speed. © 2022 Informa UK Limited, trading as Taylor & Francis Group.},
