	abstract = {Order patterns and permutation entropy have become useful tools for studying biomedical, geophysical or climate time series. Here we study day-to-day market data, and Brownian motion which is a good model for their order patterns. A crucial point is that for small lags (1 up to 6 days), pattern frequencies in financial data remain essentially constant. The two most important order parameters of a time series are turning rate and up-down balance. For change points in EEG brain data, turning rate is excellent while for financial data, up-down balance seems the best. The fit of Brownian motion with respect to these parameters is tested, providing a new version of a forgotten test by Bienaymé. © 2020, The Author(s).},
