	abstract = {This paper proposes a new structural change point detection method for time series using our new matrix decomposition method. We propose YMN decomposition which decomposes one time-series data matrix into a large random matrix and a sparse matrix. YMN decomposition can obtain the information about the latent structure from the sparse matrix. Thus our structural change point detection method using YMN decomposition can detect the change in higher-order moments of a mixing matrix as well as typical structural changes such as the change in mean, variance, and autocorrelation of time series. We also partly theorize our methods using existing theories of random matrix and statistics. Our experiment using artificial data demonstrates the effectiveness of our change point detection techniques and our experiment using real data demonstrates that our methods can detect structural changes in economics and finance. © 2019 Copyright held by the author(s).},
