	abstract = {A mean likelihood estimate of the change-point in the structure of a model generating a stochastic sequence left brace x//t right brace is expressed explicitly by means of the model's parameters, changing abruptly from THETA **(**1**) to THETA **(**2**) and observations x//1, x//2,. . . , x//n. For large n the asymptotic unbiasedness and normality of the derived estimate are proved under some additional assumptions. The quantity, determining the accuracy of the change-point estimation as well as the probability of misclassification of two stationary sequences with parameters THETA **(**1**) and THETA **(**2**), has been revealed. It is suggested to consider it as a natural measure of discernibility in the problems of recognition, classification and detection of change in time-series.},
